# CrewCut 6-film dataset (task-maker)
Commands (numbered, each with its check) in `tools/`; decisions in `decisions/`; data in `data/`.

| step | command | check | result |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 masters | tools/fetch_masters.py | SHA-256 + size of 6 masters | data/masters_check.json (6/6 OK) |
| 2 cuts | tools/step2_cuts.sh (reference `cuts`, unmodified) | step 4 | |
| 3 dialogue | tools/step3_dialogue.py, step3_run.sh | 0 lines in all 4 spoken films (same as reference) | annotations/*/dialogue.json |
| 4 shots | tools/step4_shots.py | identical to reference shots.json for 6/6 films | |
| 5 hierarchy | tools/step5_hier.sh, step5b_format.py (reference `hierarchy`, `tasks`) | hierarchy.json identical to reference 6/6 | |
| 6 descriptions | tools/step6a_frames.py, step6b_describe.py, step6b_run.sh | 603/603 shots answered, 0 empty (decisions/D003; D001 superseded) | annotations/*/descriptions.json, describe_log.jsonl |
| 7 fingerprints | tools/fingerprint.py, step7_fingerprints.sh | self-check reports reuse; negative control passes | annotations/*/fingerprint_* |
| 8 tasks/packages/key | tools/step8_tasks.py, tools/leak_scan.py | 598 task ids = reference dev.jsonl exactly; no key in packages | tasks/dev.jsonl, packages/, key/ |
| 9 clips | tools/step9_clips.py | duration within tolerance | release (large files) |

`key/` is the answer key (scoring/audit only): it must not be uploaded with the dataset or put in any release. `toolservice/` is the tool service (tool list, official prices with date and source, source-side rejection check, per-call ledger).
